{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards (collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257) in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. This is **Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION)** following a `PLAN.md` written by a planning agent. Critical contract details:\n   - The contract is the **requirements** (`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt`), NOT the plan. The plan is a guide/hypothesis to verify, not obey. When deviating from PLAN.md, jot a one-line note in PLAN.md.\n   - Use **TDD**: write one failing test through the public interface (`test_utils`), watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time). Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - Validate against requirements via throwaway real-engine smoke checks; reuse nearest FDN seam before adding anything new.\n   - Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - **Guardrails (verbatim-important):** \"Test the real engine, never a stand-in: don't hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call `on_resolve()` directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"After each card and after any `engine/` change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a change that regresses it.\" \"Do not modify anything under `engine_tests/` (the grader uses its own authoritative copies).\"\n   - From AGENTS.md (verbatim-important constraints): \"Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only\" and \"do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`\" — \"Editing them ... will not change your score, it will only mislead you.\" \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions ... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, stack (LIFO), triggered abilities, replacement effects, continuous effects (7-layer system), combat, mana payment, planeswalker loyalty abilities, activated/mana abilities.\n   - TDD red-green-refactor, vertical tracer-bullet slicing.\n   - Converge (colors of mana spent), Casualty, Counterspell, Affinity, Surveil, Miracle, Prepared, Paradigm, Land animation, coin flips / skip turns.\n   - `Keyword` is an `enum.Flag` (FLYING, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH, HASTE, etc.); `CardType` enum; `ManaType` enum (incl. COLORLESS); `ManaCost.parse(\"{N}{C}...\")` with `.cmc` and `.generic`/`.pips`.\n   - `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` for targeting.\n   - `DeterministicPlayer` pops answers from a script deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **PLAN.md** (`/workspace/PLAN.md`): Defines gaps G1–G11. Key seams to build first: G1 (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in combat.py declare_attackers_step after `attacker.is_attacking=True`), G2 (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` in casting.py cast_spell after payment), G3 (add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with `phase` field to events.py, fire in turn.py run_turn at main phases), G7 (`surveil` helper), G8 (`counter_spell` helper in stack.py). Implementation order: seams → sos_4 (converge) → sos_226 (casualty) → sos_57 (counter) → sos_1 → sos_245 → sos_97 → sos_13 → sos_120 → sos_201 → sos_257.\n   - **engine/events.py**: `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` and `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` are DEFINED but NEVER FIRED. `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` with `.card` property; subclasses `CreatureDiesReplacementEvent`, `SacrificeReplacementEvent`. `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` exist. Need to ADD `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase)`.\n   - **engine/casting.py**: `cast_spell` (line 126) sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` at line 229 after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)` (line 225); calls on_cast, pushes StackObject. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (line 254) for free casts from any zone. `get_cost_reduction` (line 89) calls `card.cost_reduction(game)`, clamps to `[0, generic]`. G2 plan: after payment, set `card.mana_spent` = actual mana paid (compute via `player.mana_pool.total()` before/after pay) and fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`.\n   - **engine/stack.py**: `StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability)`. `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` (line 72) shallow-copies source card, returns StackObject (no zone movement). `Stack` has `_items` (last=top), `push/pop/peek/objects/is_empty`. Need to ADD `Stack.remove(obj)` method and `counter_spell(game, stack_object)` helper (G8).\n   - **engine/zones.py**: `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)` (line 179) handles trigger/replacement registration. Fires ETB **before** `register_triggers`. Clears `colors_spent` on zone change. `move_zone` low-level.\n   - **engine/combat.py**: `declare_attackers_step` (line 208); at line 252 sets `attacker.is_attacking=True` and taps unless vigilance — **fires no event** (G1 inserts AttacksTriggeredEvent fire here, with `creature=attacker, attacker=defending`).\n   - **engine/turn.py**: `run_turn` (line 175) loop; upkeep fires event at line 204. Main phases `(PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)` / `(POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)` fire nothing (G3 adds elif). `_do_untap_step` clears summoning sickness, resets land_plays. Cleanup calls `effect_manager.apply_all`.\n   - **engine/game_state.py**: `advance_phase` (line 132) handles turn rotation via `extra_turns` queue and `_normal_next_index`. `_TURN_SEQUENCE` defined. For G9 skip-turns: plan to add `self.skipped_turns: dict[int,int] = {}` to `__init__` and handle in run_turn.\n   - **engine/game.py**: helpers `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card` (increments `cards_drawn_this_turn`, NEVER reset between turns; fires `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`), `discard`, `create_token`, `add_counter`, `remove_counter`. G7 surveil helper to be added here.\n   - **engine/mana.py**: `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (sorted distinct non-colorless Colors of last pay), `add(mana_type, amount)`, `total()`, `pay(cost, choices=None)`, `empty()`.\n   - **engine/continuous_effects.py**: `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, `Layer` (TYPE=4, ABILITY=6, POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), `SubLayer.MODIFY_PT`/`SET_PT`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`, `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`. `apply_all` resets to base then reapplies — ONLY called during cleanup.\n   - **engine/card.py**: `CardImpl` hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`. `Creature(base_power, base_toughness)` with `.power`/`.toughness` properties (`modified_power + plus_one - minus_one`), `_reset_characteristics`. `Instant`/`Sorcery`/`Enchantment`/`Artifact`/`Planeswalker(starting_loyalty)`/`Land` (`can_cast` returns False, `get_mana_abilities`). `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description)`, `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)`.\n   - **engine/abilities.py**: `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source, controller, loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `ActivatedAbilityInstance`, `activate_ability(game, player, ability)`, `tap_cost(game, source)`. Loyalty: sorcery-speed only, once-per-turn via `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set, `clear_loyalty_tracking()`.\n   - **engine/triggers.py**: `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`; `game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(source)/fire_event`. fire_event matches by isinstance, APNAP-ordered, pushes StackObjects, returns early (no-op) if no matching triggers.\n   - **engine/replacement_effects.py**: `ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller)`; `game.replacement_manager.register/apply`.\n   - **FDN reference cards**: fdn_245 (Ruby — `register_triggers` with AttacksTriggeredEvent + ContinuousEffect P/T buff + mana abilities); fdn_244 (Progenitus — `register_replacement_effects` with MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent, sets `event.prevented=True`); fdn_205 (Wardens — converge reads `colors_spent`, `create_token`); fdn_134 (Ajani — `get_loyalty_abilities` returns LoyaltyAbility list using `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\")`); fdn_6/fdn_57 (cost_reduction hook); fdn_13 (TargetRequirement + chosen_targets); fdn_215 (modal `get_modes`/`chosen_mode`).\n   - **FDN tests** (fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_13, fdn_244): show testing pattern — construct card with owner/controller, call `card.on_resolve(game)` or `card.register_replacement_effects(game)` directly, set `card.chosen_targets`/`colors_spent` directly, use `create_game()` from test_utils.\n   - **test_utils.py**: `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=(s1,s2))`, `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)`, `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` (scripts targets, casts via engine, auto-resolves ENTIRE stack via `_resolve_top_of_stack` which pops+on_resolve+SBA loop), `advance_to_phase(game, phase, step)` (just calls advance_phase, fires no turn actions), `declare_attackers(game, names)`, `declare_blockers(game, {attacker: [blockers]})`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors yet — still in exploration/planning phase. Baseline engine tests confirmed passing (1145 passed).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Determined `apply_all` only runs during cleanup, so continuous P