y any files under workspace/engine_tests/.\"\n   - (System reminders about deferred tools and skills availability.)\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Build shared engine seams: G1 (AttacksTriggeredEvent), G2 (SpellCastTriggeredEvent + mana_spent), G3 (BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent), G7 (surveil helper), G8 (counter_spell helper).\n   - Implement all 10 cards in order: sos_4, sos_226, sos_57, sos_1, sos_245, sos_97, sos_13, sos_120, sos_201, sos_257, each with tests.py.\n   - Run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after each engine change and each card; never regress.\n   - For sos_97 (-7) and others needing G9: add `game.skipped_turns` + skip-turn handling in run_turn, plus a coin-flip helper.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I had completed full codebase exploration and established the baseline (1145 engine tests passing). I created 11 tracking tasks. I was about to begin implementing the shared engine seams, starting with G1 — firing `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in `engine/combat.py`'s `declare_attackers_step` after `attacker.is_attacking = True` (line ~252), with `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=defending)`. I had just loaded the TaskUpdate tool and stated: \"Now I'll implement the shared engine seams. Starting with G1 (fire AttacksTriggeredEvent in combat).\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin implementing the shared engine seams (Task #1), starting with G1. In `engine/combat.py` `declare_attackers_step`, after `attacker.is_attacking = True` (line 252), add `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=defending))` (importing `AttacksTriggeredEvent` from `engine.events`). Then proceed to G2 (casting.py: record `card.mana_spent` via mana-pool delta and fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` after payment in `cast_spell`), G3 (add `Beginni