{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DyfQTagivd5DUqvaUXbFxv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PLAN.md — SOS card implementation handoff\n2\t\n3\tThis is the **complete** handoff for the implementation agent. You have not seen the\n4\tresearch that produced this; everything you need is here plus the files it points at.\n5\t\n6\tCards to implement (10): **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\n7\tEach lives at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (a bare stub today) with a\n8\t`card_spec.json` beside it. Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n9\t\n10\t## Hard rules (from AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n11\t- **Engine: additive only.** You may add files/classes/methods/helpers in `engine/`\n12\t  and may edit the *bodies* of existing functions. You MUST NOT rename, move, or\n13\t  delete anything existing in `engine/`. No refactors.\n14\t- Keep each card's class in `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py`. Don't move card dirs.\n15\t- `engine_tests/` and `cards/fdn/**/tests.py` are **read-only** (read FDN tests as\n16\t  examples; never edit/add). The grader uses its own copies.\n17\t- Rules questions: grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (use `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`); don't read it whole.\n18\t- Run tests with `pytest` from the workspace root.\n19\t\n20\t## Engine facts you must rely on (verified — file:line)\n21\t- **Cast pipeline** `engine/casting.py`:\n22\t  - `cast_spell(game, player, card)` (line 126): timing → `can_cast` → hand→stack →\n23\t    `get_targets`/choose → pay mana → `on_cast` → push `StackObject`. After payment it sets\n24\t    `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (line 229). It does\n25\t    **not** fire any \"spell cast\" event and does **not** record total mana paid.\n26\t  - `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (line 254): no timing/mana; moves card\n27\t    from `from_zone`→stack, chooses+validates targets (with rollback), `on_cast`, pushes a\n28\t    `StackObject` that resolves normally (permanents→battlefield, others→graveyard). Works\n29\t    from exile/graveyard/library. Use this for all \"cast without paying\" effects.\n30\t  - `get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` (line 89): calls `card.cost_reduction(game)`,\n31\t    clamps result into `[0, mana_cost.generic]` (never reduces colored pips). Self-reduction only.\n32\t- **Copies** `engine/stack.py`: `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` (line 72)\n33\t  shallow-copies the source card, returns a `StackObject` whose `on_resolve` calls the copy's\n34\t  `on_resolve` (no zone movement — correct for copies). Push it with `game.stack.push(...)`.\n35\t- **Triggers** `engine/triggers.py`: register with\n36\t  `game.trigger_manager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type=<EventClass>, condition=fn_or_None,\n37\t  effect=fn, source=self, controller=ctrl))`. `fire_event(game, event)` matches by `isinstance`\n38\t  (subclasses included), APNAP-ordered, pushes `StackObject`s. `unregister(source)` removes by identity.\n39\t  - `move_to_zone` (`engine/zones.py:314`) calls `card.register_triggers(game)` on enter and\n40\t    `unregister(card)` on leave (line 298), and clears stale `colors_spent` (line 160). So a\n41\t    permanent's `register_triggers` is the canonical place to wire battlefield triggers.\n42\t  - Pattern to copy: `cards/fdn/fdn_245/card_impl.py` (registers an `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger).\n43\t- **Events** `engine/events.py`: these dataclasses already exist but note firing status:\n44\t  - `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` (line 97) — **defined, never fired**.\n45\t  - `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` (line 105) — **defined, never fired**.\n46\t  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)` (line 64) — **IS fired** by `game.draw_card` (game.py:332).\n47\t  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (line 70) — fired in `run_turn` (turn.py:204).\n48\t  - No \"beginning of main phase\" event exists.\n49\t  - Replacement base `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(... destination, prevented)` (line 132); set\n50\t    `event.prevented=True` + redirect `destination` to override a graveyard move. Pattern:\n51\t    `cards/fdn/fdn_244/card_impl.py` (`register_replacement_effects`).\n52\t- **Turn loop** `engine/turn.py:175 run_turn`: per step it does turn actions then `priority_loop`.\n53\t  Upkeep fires its event (line 204); main phases (`Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n54\t  `Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN`, `engine/types.py:56-58`) fire nothing.\n55\t- **Combat** `engine/combat.py:208 declare_attackers_step`: sets `attacker.is_attacking=True`\n56\t  and taps (unless vigilance) at line 252; **fires no event**.\n57\t- **Draw tracking** `engine/game.py:294 draw_card`: increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`\n58\t  (line 326) but it is **never reset between turns** — reset it yourself for \"first draw\" logic.\n59\t- **Mana** `engine/mana.py`: `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (line 57) = sorted distinct non-colorless\n60\t  `Color`s of the last `pay`. No per-mana \"spend only on X\" restriction support exists.\n61\t- **Cost reduction hook** examples: `cards/fdn/fdn_57` and `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (affinity-style count).\n62\t- **Converge** example: `cards/fdn/fdn_205` — reads colors spent in `on_resolve`. Real pipeline\n63\t  stores a **list**, so always compute `X = len(getattr(card, \"colors_spent\", []))`.\n64\t- **Planeswalker** example: `cards/fdn/fdn_134` — `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n65\t  `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost:int, effect:callable, description:str)` (`engine/card.py:60`).\n66\t  `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities` (card.py:471). Activation/once-per-turn machinery in\n67\t  `engine/abilities.py` (`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`).\n68\t- **Mana abilities / land** pattern: `engine/basic_lands.py`; `Land.can_cast` returns False,\n69\t  override `get_mana_abilities()` / `get_activated_abilities()`.\n70\t- **Continuous effects** `engine/continuous_effects.py`: `Layer.TYPE=4`, `Layer.ABILITY=6`,\n71\t  `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7`; `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, duration)` via\n72\t  `game.effect_manager.add(...)`. `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`, `DURATION_PERMANENT`. Example:\n73\t  `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (end-of-turn P/T buff).\n74\t- **Test helpers** `test_utils.py`: `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=...)`,\n75\t  `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)`,\n76\t  `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`,\n77\t  `declare_blockers`. Scripted choices via `DeterministicPlayer` (engine/player.py).\n78\t\n79\t---\n80\t\n81\t## Section 1 — Engine gaps table\n82\t\n83\tPrefer building the **shared seams (G1–G3)** once; most cards hang off them.\n84\t\n85\t| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n86\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n87\t| G1 | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" trigger fires | In `declare_attackers_step`, after `attacker.is_attacking=True`, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=defending))` | `engine/combat.py:252` (event already exists) | **sos_1** (also fixes latent fdn_245) |\n88\t| G2 | \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" + record mana paid | In `cast_spell`, after pushing the `StackObject`, set `card.mana_spent = <total mana actually paid>` and `fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stackobj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))` | `engine/casting.py` (~after line 229; event exists) | **sos_257**, **sos_226**, **sos_57** (reads `mana_spent`) |\n89\t| G3 | \"At the beginning of your (next/first) main phase\" trigger | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with a `phase` field in `engine/events.py`; fire it in `run_turn` when `current[0] in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN)` | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py:~207` (new `elif` branch before priority_loop) | **sos_57**, **sos_120** |\n90\t| G4 | Cast a copy of a spell (casualty / paradigm / prepared) | Reuse existing `copy_spell`; add tiny wrapper `cast_copy(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None)` that builds via `copy_spell` and `game.stack.push`es it | `engine/stack.py:72` (exists) | **sos_226**, **sos_120**, **sos_13** |\n91\t| G5 | Cast for free from graveyard/exile + \"if it would go to graveyard, exile instead\" | Reuse `cast_spell_free`; for the redirect, register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` effect on that card (set `prevented=True`, move to exile) à la fdn_244 | `engine/casting.py:254` + `engine/replacement_effects.py` (both exist) | **sos_1**, **sos_120** |\n92\t| G6 | Grant cost reduction to *other* spells you cast (affinity granted) | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `card.cost_reduction`, also add reductions from controller's permanents that expose a `grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)->int` hook; sum then clamp to generic | `engine/casting.py:89` (edit body, additive) | **sos_245** |\n93\t| G7 | Surveil N | Add helper `surveil(game, player, n)` in a new `engine/library_ops.py` (or `engine/game.py`): look at top N, let `player` choose any subset to graveyard, keep rest on top in chosen order | new helper (additive) | **sos_97** (also fits fdn_49/53) |\n94\t| G8 | Counter target spell | Add helper `counter_spell(game, stack_object)` in `engine/stack.py`: remove the `StackObject` from `game.stack`, move its `source` card to owner's graveyard via `move_to_zone` | `engine/stack.py` (new fn, additive) | **sos_57** |\n95\t| G9 | \"Skips their next X turns\" + coin flips | Add `game.skipped_turns: dict[int,int]` (seat→count); at top of `run_turn`, if `skipped_turns.get(active_idx,0)>0`, decrement and `advance` straight to next turn (no phases/priority). Add `flip_coin(game, player)->bool` helper (seedable / player-scriptable) | `engine/game_state.py` + `engine/turn.py` (edit bodies) | **sos_97** (−7 only) |\n96\t| G10 | Miracle (cast first-drawn card for alt cost) | Reset `player.cards_drawn_this_turn=0` each turn (in `_do_untap_step` or `run_turn`). Add `cast_for_cost(game, player, card, ManaCost)` = `cast_spell` path with a temporarily-overridden `mana_cost`. Lorehold registers a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger | `engine/game.py`/`turn.py` reset + `engine/casting.py` helper | **sos_201** |\n97\t| G11 | Land becomes a creature; restricted mana | Animation = permanent `ContinuousEffect`s: `Layer.TYPE` add `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype \"Wizard\", `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` set 2/4, plus register its cast-trigger. Restricted mana: tag the produced mana (e.g. `mana_pool.add(..., restriction=\"instant_sorcery\")`) — **minimal** support; if the pool can't carry tags, simplify (see sos_257 notes) | `engine/continuous_effects.py` (reuse) + `engine/mana.py` (optional tag) | **sos_257** |\n98\t\n99\t---\n100\t\n101\t## Section 2 — Per-card plan\n102\t\n103\tFor every card: change the stub's base class (currently `class X(CardImpl): pass`), set\n104\t`name/mana_cost/type_line/power/toughness/subtypes/supertypes/keywords` in `__init__` via\n105\t`kwargs.setdefault(...)` (copy an FDN `__init__`), then implement the hooks below.\n106\t\n107\t### sos_4 — Together as One — Sorcery {6} — Converge (EASIEST; no engine change)\n108\t- **Clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life,\n109\t  X = number of colors of mana spent.\"\n110\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (converge).\n111\t- **Seams:** none new. `colors_spent` is already set by `cast_spell`.\n112\t- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `get_targets` → two requirements: (a) a player, (b) \"any target\"\n113\t  (creature OR player OR planeswalker; use a `TargetRequirement` with a filter). `on_resolve`:\n114\t  `X = len(getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", []))`; `game.draw_card` X times for target player;\n115\t  `game.deal_damage(source=self, target=second, amount=X)`; `controller gains X life`.\n116\t- **Edge/tests:** X can be 0 (all-colorless payment) → all three do nothing harmful;\n117\t  X=3 (three colors) draws 3 / 3 dmg / +3 life; damage target may be a player or creature.\n118\t  To force colors in a test, set `mana=` to several colors and pay generic with them.\n119\t\n120\t### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant — Creature {2}{W}{B} 4/4 — Casualty grant (uses G2,G4)\n121\t- **Clauses:** Flying, vigilance (existing keywords). \"Each instant/sorcery spell you cast has\n122\t  casualty 1 (as you cast, may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you do, copy the spell,\n123\t  may choose new targets).\"\n124\t- **Analogue:** trigger wiring `cards/fdn/fdn_245`; copy via `engine/stack.py:copy_spell`.\n125\t- **Seams:** **G2** (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`), **G4** (`cast_copy`).\n126\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`. In `register_triggers`,\n127\t  register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger, `source=self`, `controller=self.controller`,\n128\t  condition = (event.controller is self.controller) AND event card has `CardType.INSTANT` or\n129\t  `CardType.SORCERY`. Effect: ask `controller.choose_yes_no` (\"pay casualty?\"); if yes, pick a\n130\t  controlled creature with power≥1, `game.sacrifice` it, then `cast_copy(game, event.spell,\n131\t  controller, new_targets=<player picks>)`.\n132\t- **Edge/tests:** no creature to sac, or decline → no copy, original still resolves; copy can\n133\t  retarget; a *non* instant/sorcery cast (a creature) does not trigger; only the controller's\n134\t  casts trigger, not the opponent's. (Simplification vs real \"as-you-cast\" timing is acceptable —\n135\t  copy happens right after the spell hits the stack.)\n136\t\n137\t### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt — Instant {1}{U}{U} — Counterspell (uses G2 mana_spent, G3, G8)\n138\t- **Clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount of mana\n139\t  spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n140\t- **Analogue:** counter — none ships with a test; build on G8. Scheduling — G3.\n141\t- **Seams:** **G8** (`counter_spell`), **G2** (read `event/card.mana_spent`), **G3** (next main phase).\n142\t- **Impl:** base `Instant`. `get_targets` → one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` selecting a\n143\t  `StackObject` (filter to spells). `on_resolve`: read the targeted stack object; capture\n144\t  `amount = getattr(target.source, \"mana_spent\", target.source.mana_cost.cmc)`; `counter_spell`.\n145\t  Then if controller's battlefield has a creature with \"Wizard\" in `subtypes`: register a one-shot\n146\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (controller=you) that on its next firing adds\n147\t  `amount` {C} to `controller.mana_pool` and unregisters itself (`source` = a unique sentinel obj\n148\t  you keep a handle to).\n149\t- **Edge/tests:** target already gone (fizzle) → counter nothing; no Wizard → just counter, no\n150\t  mana; with Wizard → exactly `amount` {C} appears at your next main phase, once. For the test,\n151\t  cast a dummy spell, respond with Mana Sculpt, resolve, assert target moved to graveyard and (with\n152\t  a Wizard on board) mana pool gains {C} at the following main phase.\n153\t\n154\t### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic — Creature {10} 7/7 — attack recast (uses G1, G5)\n155\t- **Clauses:** \"Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever it\n156\t  attacks, you may cast target instant/sorcery from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\n157\t  If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n158\t- **Analogue:** cost reduction `cards/fdn/fdn_57`/`fdn_6`; attack trigger `cards/fdn/fdn_245`;\n159\t  graveyard redirect `cards/fdn/fdn_244`.\n160\t- **Seams:** **G1** (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`), **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from graveyard +\n161\t  one-shot exile-instead-of-graveyard replacement).\n162\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.REACH`, base P/T 7/7. `cost_reduction(game)` =\n163\t  count of cards in controller's graveyard whose `card_types` include INSTANT or SORCERY (engine\n164\t  clamps to the {10} generic). `register_triggers`: `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, condition\n165\t  `event.creature is self`, effect = `choose_yes_no` then pick a target instant/sorcery in your\n166\t  graveyard, register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` on that card (redirect to exile),\n167\t  then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n168\t- **Edge/tests:** cost is {10} minus graveyard count, floored at 0 colored pips (none here);\n169\t  attacking with empty graveyard / declining → nothing cast; the recast spell, after resolving,\n170\t  goes to **exile** not graveyard (assert zone). Use `declare_attackers` helper to fire G1.\n171\t\n172\t### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer — Creature {6}{B}{G} 5/5 — Affinity (uses G6)\n173\t- **Clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control). Flying,\n174\t  deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n175\t- **Analogue:** self-affinity `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n176\t- **Seams:** self-part = `cost_reduction` hook (no engine change). Grant-to-others = **G6**.\n177\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`. `cost_reduction(game)` =\n178\t  number of creatures controller controls. Add a `grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`\n179\t  method returning `creature_count` **iff** `card` has INSTANT/SORCERY type and is controlled by\n180\t  the same player; G6 makes `get_cost_reduction` poll this across the battlefield.\n181\t- **Edge/tests:** self cast cost drops by creature count (e.g. 3 creatures → {3}{B}{G}); an\n182\t  instant you cast while Witherbloom is out is cheaper by creature count; a creature spell is not\n183\t  affected; reduction never eats colored pips. Witherbloom counts itself? It's not yet on the\n184\t  battlefield while being cast, so self-cast counts only *other* creatures — match RULEBOOK.\n185\t\n186\t### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — Planeswalker {1}{B}{B}, loyalty 3 (uses G7, G9)\n187\t- **Clauses:** `+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card. −2: Return\n188\t  target creature card with MV ≤3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins;\n189\t  target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).`\n190\t- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_134` (loyalty abilities + targeting).\n191\t- **Seams:** **G7** (surveil) for +1; existing `discard`/`choose_card` for −1; existing\n192\t  `move_to_zone`→battlefield for −2; **G9** (skip turns + coin flips) for −7.\n193\t- **Impl:** base `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3)`, `supertypes={LEGENDARY}`, subtype \"Ral\".\n194\t  `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility(+1/−1/−2/−7, effect, desc)`.\n195\t  - +1: `surveil(game, controller, 2)`.\n196\t  - −1: choose any number of target players; each chosen player `choose_card` from hand → `discard`.\n197\t  - −2: target a creature card in controller's graveyard with `mana_cost.cmc ≤ 3`; `move_to_zone`\n198\t    it to controller's battlefield.\n199\t  - −7: `heads = sum(flip_coin(game, controller) for _ in range(5))`; target opponent;\n200\t    `game.skipped_turns[opp_seat] += heads`.\n201\t- **Edge/tests:** loyalty arithmetic and sorcery-speed/once-per-turn already handled by\n202\t  `engine/abilities.py`; test +1 surveil moves chosen cards to graveyard / keeps order; −2 only\n203\t  legal for MV≤3 creature cards; −7 with scripted coin results skips exactly that many of the\n204\t  opponent's turns (drive turns with `run_turn`). **−7 is the hardest part — do it last** (G9).\n205\t\n206\t### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — {1}{W}{W} 3/3 // {W} — Prepared (uses G4)\n207\t- **Clauses (front face, the creature):** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 W/B\n208\t  Inkling with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared.\n209\t  (While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so unprepares it.)\" The \"spell\" = the\n210\t  `// Swords to Plowshares` half: `{W}` Instant — \"Exile target creature; its controller gains\n211\t  life equal to its power.\"\n212\t- **Analogue:** ETB token `cards/fdn` token-makers; copy via `copy_spell`/**G4**.\n213\t- **Seams:** **G4** (cast a copy), `create_token`, replacement-free.\n214\t- **Impl:** implement the **creature** as the canonical class (`Creature`, {1}{W}{W}, 3/3,\n215\t  subtypes {Cat, Cleric}). `register_triggers` → `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` condition\n216\t  `event card is self`: target player creates `1/1 white/black Inkling, flying` via\n217\t  `game.create_token`; then if any opponent controls more creatures than controller, set\n218\t  `self.prepared=True`. Provide the StP effect as a method `_stp_resolve(game, target_creature)`:\n219\t  `game.exile(target)`, target's controller gains life = target's power. Expose a special action /\n220\t  `get_activated_abilities` available while `self.prepared` and on battlefield (instant speed, no\n221\t  mana — it's \"cast a copy ... without paying\") that targets a creature, runs `_stp_resolve`, and\n222\t  sets `self.prepared=False`.\n223\t- **Edge/tests:** ETB always makes the token; `prepared` only set when opponent has strictly more\n224\t  creatures; using the prepared action exiles a creature, grants life = power, and clears\n225\t  `prepared` (can't be used twice without re-preparing). **Ambiguous card** — keep the\n226\t  interpretation above; if a staged test disagrees, adjust the trigger/special-action shape, not\n227\t  the engine. Complex — schedule late.\n228\t\n229\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone — Sorcery — Lesson {5}{R}{R} — Paradigm (uses G3, G5, G4)\n230\t- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of library until you exile cards with total MV ≥4. You may\n231\t  cast any number of them without paying. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n232\t  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying at the beginning of\n233\t  each of your first main phases.)\"\n234\t- **Analogue:** free-cast `cast_spell_free`; scheduling `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n235\t- **Seams:** **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from exile), **G3** (first main phase trigger), **G4/G5** (cast copy from exile).\n236\t- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop top of controller's library into exile, summing\n237\t  `mana_cost.cmc`, until sum ≥4 (or library empty); for each exiled card the controller may\n238\t  `cast_spell_free(... from Zone.EXILE)`. **Paradigm:** override the spell's own move-to-graveyard\n239\t  so it goes to exile instead (one-shot replacement, like sos_1); set a per-player flag\n240\t  `controller.paradigm_<thisname>=True`; register a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger\n241\t  (condition: controller's **precombat** main, i.e. event.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN and active player is\n242\t  controller) that each turn offers to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n243\t  (`cast_copy` of a fresh `StackObject`, or simply `cast_spell_free` a `copy.copy` from exile).\n244\t- **Edge/tests:** stops as soon as total MV ≥4 (single MV-5 card stops immediately); casting the\n245\t  exiled spells is optional and any subset; after first resolution the card sits in exile and a\n246\t  copy becomes castable at each of your first main phases. Expert — schedule late.\n247\t\n248\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 — Miracle grant (uses G10)\n249\t- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2} (cast it\n250\t  when you draw it if it's the first card drawn this turn, for {2}). At the beginning of each\n251\t  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n252\t- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n253\t- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n254\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n255\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n256\t  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n257\t  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n258\t    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n259\t    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n260\t  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n261\t    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n262\t- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n263\t  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n264\t  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n265\t\n266\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n267\t- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n268\t  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n269\t  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n270\t- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n271\t- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n272\t  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n273\t- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n274\t  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n275\t  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n276\t    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n277\t    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n278\t  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n279\t  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n280\t  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n281\t  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n282\t- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n283\t  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n284\t  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n285\t  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n286\t\n287\t---\n288\t\n289\t## Section 3 — Implementation order\n290\t\n291\tBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\n292\tsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n293\t\n294\t**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n295\t1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n296\t2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n297\t   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n298\t3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n299\t4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n300\t   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n301\t   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n302\t\n303\t**Group A — no/low new engine (warm-up):**\n304\t5. **sos_4** (Converge) — pure `on_resolve`; nothing new. *Validates targeting + colors_spent.*\n305\t6. **sos_226** (casualty) — G2 + `copy_spell`. *First consumer of the cast trigger.*\n306\t7. **sos_57** (Mana Sculpt) — G8 + G2(`mana_spent`) + G3. *Exercises counter + scheduled mana.*\n307\t\n308\t**Group B — graveyard/exile recasting & cost grants:**\n309\t8. **sos_1** (Dawning Archaic) — G1 + G5 (free-cast + exile redirect). *Cost reduction + attack recast.*\n310\t9. **sos_245** (Witherbloom) — `cost_reduction` self + G6 grant. *Cost-system extension.*\n311\t\n312\t**Group C — planeswalker (modes mostly easy; ultimate hard):**\n313\t10. **sos_97** (Ral) — +1/−1/−2 via G7/discard/move (easy); **−7 via G9 last** (skip turns + coins).\n314\t\n315\t**Group D — hardest (copy/alt-cost/animation):**\n316\t11. **sos_13** (Prepared) — G4 + ETB token + special action; ambiguous, isolate it.\n317\t12. **sos_120** (Paradigm) — G3 + G5 + G4; exile-recast scheduling.\n318\t13. **sos_201** (Lorehold/Miracle) — G10 (draw trigger + per-turn reset + alt-cost cast).\n319\t14. **sos_257** (Great Hall) — G11 land animation + restricted mana + G2 trigger.\n320\t\n321\t*Rationale for ordering:* Group A proves the three core seams (G1–G3, G7, G8) against simple\n322\ton-resolve logic before anything depends on them in combination. Group B reuses the free-cast and\n323\tcost-reduction machinery. The planeswalker is mid-pack because three of its four modes are trivial\n324\tonce G7 exists; its ultimate (G9) is the one genuinely new subsystem, so defer it. Group D cards\n325\teach introduce a self-contained hard mechanic (copying a spell, alt-cost casting on draw, type-layer\n326\tanimation) and benefit from all earlier seams being stable.\n327\t\n328\t## Testing notes (apply throughout)\n329\t- Put tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`; import `from cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <Class>`\n330\t  and `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state`.\n331\t- Use `DeterministicPlayer` scripts (via `create_game(..., scripts=...)`) to make `choose_*`,\n332\t  coin flips, and \"may\" prompts deterministic.\n333\t- After each engine seam, run `pytest` — `engine_tests/` must stay green (they're authoritative-style\n334\t  regressions; your additive changes should not break them).\n335\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"6831e90f-f72a-410e-bb01-25172872dbb0","timestamp":"2026-06-04T02:41:26.627Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"# PLAN.md — SOS card implementation handoff\n\nThis is the **complete** handoff for the implementation agent. You have not seen the\nresearch that produced this; everything you need is here plus the files it points at.\n\nCards to implement (10): **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**.\nEach lives at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (a bare stub today) with a\n`card_spec.json` beside it. Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n## Hard rules (from AGENTS.md — do not violate)\n- **Engine: additive only.** You may add files/classes/methods/helpers in `engine/`\n  and may edit the *bodies* of existing functions. You MUST NOT rename, move, or\n  delete anything existing in `engine/`. No refactors.\n- Keep each card's class in `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py`. Don't move card dirs.\n- `engine_tests/` and `cards/fdn/**/tests.py` are **read-only** (read FDN tests as\n  examples; never edit/add). The grader uses its own copies.\n- Rules questions: grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (use `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`); don't read it whole.\n- Run tests with `pytest` from the workspace root.\n\n## Engine facts you must rely on (verified — file:line)\n- **Cast pipeline** `engine/casting.py`:\n  - `cast_spell(game, player, card)` (line 126): timing → `can_cast` → hand→stack →\n    `get_targets`/choose → pay mana → `on_cast` → push `StackObject`. After payment it sets\n    `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` (line 229). It does\n    **not** fire any \"spell cast\" event and does **not** record total mana paid.\n  - `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (line 254): no timing/mana; moves card\n    from `from_zone`→stack, chooses+validates targets (with rollback), `on_cast`, pushes a\n    `StackObject` that resolves normally (permanents→battlefield, others→graveyard). Works\n    from exile/graveyard/library. Use this for all \"cast without paying\" effects.\n  - `get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` (line 89): calls `card.cost_reduction(game)`,\n    clamps result into `[0, mana_cost.generic]` (never reduces colored pips). Self-reduction only.\n- **Copies** `engine/stack.py`: `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` (line 72)\n  shallow-copies the source card, returns a `StackObject` whose `on_resolve` calls the copy's\n  `on_resolve` (no zone movement — correct for copies). Push it with `game.stack.push(...)`.\n- **Triggers** `engine/triggers.py`: register with\n  `game.trigger_manager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type=<EventClass>, condition=fn_or_None,\n  effect=fn, source=self, controller=ctrl))`. `fire_event(game, event)` matches by `isinstance`\n  (subclasses included), APNAP-ordered, pushes `StackObject`s. `unregister(source)` removes by identity.\n  - `move_to_zone` (`engine/zones.py:314`) calls `card.register_triggers(game)` on enter and\n    `unregister(card)` on leave (line 298), and clears stale `colors_spent` (line 160). So a\n    permanent's `register_triggers` is the canonical place to wire battlefield triggers.\n  - Pattern to copy: `cards/fdn/fdn_245/card_impl.py` (registers an `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger).\n- **Events** `engine/events.py`: these dataclasses already exist but note firing status:\n  - `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` (line 97) — **defined, never fired**.\n  - `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` (line 105) — **defined, never fired**.\n  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card)` (line 64) — **IS fired** by `game.draw_card` (game.py:332).\n  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (line 70) — fired in `run_turn` (turn.py:204).\n  - No \"beginning of main phase\" event exists.\n  - Replacement base `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(... destination, prevented)` (line 132); set\n    `event.prevented=True` + redirect `destination` to override a graveyard move. Pattern:\n    `cards/fdn/fdn_244/card_impl.py` (`register_replacement_effects`).\n- **Turn loop** `engine/turn.py:175 run_turn`: per step it does turn actions then `priority_loop`.\n  Upkeep fires its event (line 204); main phases (`Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN`,\n  `Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN`, `engine/types.py:56-58`) fire nothing.\n- **Combat** `engine/combat.py:208 declare_attackers_step`: sets `attacker.is_attacking=True`\n  and taps (unless vigilance) at line 252; **fires no event**.\n- **Draw tracking** `engine/game.py:294 draw_card`: increments `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`\n  (line 326) but it is **never reset between turns** — reset it yourself for \"first draw\" logic.\n- **Mana** `engine/mana.py`: `ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (line 57) = sorted distinct non-colorless\n  `Color`s of the last `pay`. No per-mana \"spend only on X\" restriction support exists.\n- **Cost reduction hook** examples: `cards/fdn/fdn_57` and `cards/fdn/fdn_6` (affinity-style count).\n- **Converge** example: `cards/fdn/fdn_205` — reads colors spent in `on_resolve`. Real pipeline\n  stores a **list**, so always compute `X = len(getattr(card, \"colors_spent\", []))`.\n- **Planeswalker** example: `cards/fdn/fdn_134` — `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns\n  `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost:int, effect:callable, description:str)` (`engine/card.py:60`).\n  `Planeswalker.get_loyalty_abilities` (card.py:471). Activation/once-per-turn machinery in\n  `engine/abilities.py` (`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`).\n- **Mana abilities / land** pattern: `engine/basic_lands.py`; `Land.can_cast` returns False,\n  override `get_mana_abilities()` / `get_activated_abilities()`.\n- **Continuous effects** `engine/continuous_effects.py`: `Layer.TYPE=4`, `Layer.ABILITY=6`,\n  `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS=7`; `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, duration)` via\n  `game.effect_manager.add(...)`. `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`, `DURATION_PERMANENT`. Example:\n  `cards/fdn/fdn_245` (end-of-turn P/T buff).\n- **Test helpers** `test_utils.py`: `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=...)`,\n  `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)`,\n  `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`,\n  `declare_blockers`. Scripted choices via `DeterministicPlayer` (engine/player.py).\n\n---\n\n## Section 1 — Engine gaps table\n\nPrefer building the **shared seams (G1–G3)** once; most cards hang off them.\n\n| # | Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G1 | \"Whenever ~ attacks\" trigger fires | In `declare_attackers_step`, after `attacker.is_attacking=True`, call `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=defending))` | `engine/combat.py:252` (event already exists) | **sos_1** (also fixes latent fdn_245) |\n| G2 | \"Whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" + record mana paid | In `cast_spell`, after pushing the `StackObject`, set `card.mana_spent = <total mana actually paid>` and `fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stackobj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))` | `engine/casting.py` (~after line 229; event exists) | **sos_257**, **sos_226**, **sos_57** (reads `mana_spent`) |\n| G3 | \"At the beginning of your (next/first) main phase\" trigger | Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent)` with a `phase` field in `engine/events.py`; fire it in `run_turn` when `current[0] in (PRECOMBAT_MAIN, POSTCOMBAT_MAIN)` | `engine/events.py` + `engine/turn.py:~207` (new `elif` branch before priority_loop) | **sos_57**, **sos_120** |\n| G4 | Cast a copy of a spell (casualty / paradigm / prepared) | Reuse existing `copy_spell`; add tiny wrapper `cast_copy(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None)` that builds via `copy_spell` and `game.stack.push`es it | `engine/stack.py:72` (exists) | **sos_226**, **sos_120**, **sos_13** |\n| G5 | Cast for free from graveyard/exile + \"if it would go to graveyard, exile instead\" | Reuse `cast_spell_free`; for the redirect, register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` effect on that card (set `prevented=True`, move to exile) à la fdn_244 | `engine/casting.py:254` + `engine/replacement_effects.py` (both exist) | **sos_1**, **sos_120** |\n| G6 | Grant cost reduction to *other* spells you cast (affinity granted) | In `get_cost_reduction`, after `card.cost_reduction`, also add reductions from controller's permanents that expose a `grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)->int` hook; sum then clamp to generic | `engine/casting.py:89` (edit body, additive) | **sos_245** |\n| G7 | Surveil N | Add helper `surveil(game, player, n)` in a new `engine/library_ops.py` (or `engine/game.py`): look at top N, let `player` choose any subset to graveyard, keep rest on top in chosen order | new helper (additive) | **sos_97** (also fits fdn_49/53) |\n| G8 | Counter target spell | Add helper `counter_spell(game, stack_object)` in `engine/stack.py`: remove the `StackObject` from `game.stack`, move its `source` card to owner's graveyard via `move_to_zone` | `engine/stack.py` (new fn, additive) | **sos_57** |\n| G9 | \"Skips their next X turns\" + coin flips | Add `game.skipped_turns: dict[int,int]` (seat→count); at top of `run_turn`, if `skipped_turns.get(active_idx,0)>0`, decrement and `advance` straight to next turn (no phases/priority). Add `flip_coin(game, player)->bool` helper (seedable / player-scriptable) | `engine/game_state.py` + `engine/turn.py` (edit bodies) | **sos_97** (−7 only) |\n| G10 | Miracle (cast first-drawn card for alt cost) | Reset `player.cards_drawn_this_turn=0` each turn (in `_do_untap_step` or `run_turn`). Add `cast_for_cost(game, player, card, ManaCost)` = `cast_spell` path with a temporarily-overridden `mana_cost`. Lorehold registers a `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent` trigger | `engine/game.py`/`turn.py` reset + `engine/casting.py` helper | **sos_201** |\n| G11 | Land becomes a creature; restricted mana | Animation = permanent `ContinuousEffect`s: `Layer.TYPE` add `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype \"Wizard\", `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` set 2/4, plus register its cast-trigger. Restricted mana: tag the produced mana (e.g. `mana_pool.add(..., restriction=\"instant_sorcery\")`) — **minimal** support; if the pool can't carry tags, simplify (see sos_257 notes) | `engine/continuous_effects.py` (reuse) + `engine/mana.py` (optional tag) | **sos_257** |\n\n---\n\n## Section 2 — Per-card plan\n\nFor every card: change the stub's base class (currently `class X(CardImpl): pass`), set\n`name/mana_cost/type_line/power/toughness/subtypes/supertypes/keywords` in `__init__` via\n`kwargs.setdefault(...)` (copy an FDN `__init__`), then implement the hooks below.\n\n### sos_4 — Together as One — Sorcery {6} — Converge (EASIEST; no engine change)\n- **Clauses:** \"Converge — Target player draws X, deal X damage to any target, you gain X life,\n  X = number of colors of mana spent.\"\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_205` (converge).\n- **Seams:** none new. `colors_spent` is already set by `cast_spell`.\n- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `get_targets` → two requirements: (a) a player, (b) \"any target\"\n  (creature OR player OR planeswalker; use a `TargetRequirement` with a filter). `on_resolve`:\n  `X = len(getattr(self, \"colors_spent\", []))`; `game.draw_card` X times for target player;\n  `game.deal_damage(source=self, target=second, amount=X)`; `controller gains X life`.\n- **Edge/tests:** X can be 0 (all-colorless payment) → all three do nothing harmful;\n  X=3 (three colors) draws 3 / 3 dmg / +3 life; damage target may be a player or creature.\n  To force colors in a test, set `mana=` to several colors and pay generic with them.\n\n### sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant — Creature {2}{W}{B} 4/4 — Casualty grant (uses G2,G4)\n- **Clauses:** Flying, vigilance (existing keywords). \"Each instant/sorcery spell you cast has\n  casualty 1 (as you cast, may sacrifice a creature with power ≥1; when you do, copy the spell,\n  may choose new targets).\"\n- **Analogue:** trigger wiring `cards/fdn/fdn_245`; copy via `engine/stack.py:copy_spell`.\n- **Seams:** **G2** (fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`), **G4** (`cast_copy`).\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.VIGILANCE`. In `register_triggers`,\n  register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger, `source=self`, `controller=self.controller`,\n  condition = (event.controller is self.controller) AND event card has `CardType.INSTANT` or\n  `CardType.SORCERY`. Effect: ask `controller.choose_yes_no` (\"pay casualty?\"); if yes, pick a\n  controlled creature with power≥1, `game.sacrifice` it, then `cast_copy(game, event.spell,\n  controller, new_targets=<player picks>)`.\n- **Edge/tests:** no creature to sac, or decline → no copy, original still resolves; copy can\n  retarget; a *non* instant/sorcery cast (a creature) does not trigger; only the controller's\n  casts trigger, not the opponent's. (Simplification vs real \"as-you-cast\" timing is acceptable —\n  copy happens right after the spell hits the stack.)\n\n### sos_57 — Mana Sculpt — Instant {1}{U}{U} — Counterspell (uses G2 mana_spent, G3, G8)\n- **Clauses:** \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to the amount of mana\n  spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n- **Analogue:** counter — none ships with a test; build on G8. Scheduling — G3.\n- **Seams:** **G8** (`counter_spell`), **G2** (read `event/card.mana_spent`), **G3** (next main phase).\n- **Impl:** base `Instant`. `get_targets` → one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` selecting a\n  `StackObject` (filter to spells). `on_resolve`: read the targeted stack object; capture\n  `amount = getattr(target.source, \"mana_spent\", target.source.mana_cost.cmc)`; `counter_spell`.\n  Then if controller's battlefield has a creature with \"Wizard\" in `subtypes`: register a one-shot\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger (controller=you) that on its next firing adds\n  `amount` {C} to `controller.mana_pool` and unregisters itself (`source` = a unique sentinel obj\n  you keep a handle to).\n- **Edge/tests:** target already gone (fizzle) → counter nothing; no Wizard → just counter, no\n  mana; with Wizard → exactly `amount` {C} appears at your next main phase, once. For the test,\n  cast a dummy spell, respond with Mana Sculpt, resolve, assert target moved to graveyard and (with\n  a Wizard on board) mana pool gains {C} at the following main phase.\n\n### sos_1 — The Dawning Archaic — Creature {10} 7/7 — attack recast (uses G1, G5)\n- **Clauses:** \"Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery card in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever it\n  attacks, you may cast target instant/sorcery from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\n  If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"\n- **Analogue:** cost reduction `cards/fdn/fdn_57`/`fdn_6`; attack trigger `cards/fdn/fdn_245`;\n  graveyard redirect `cards/fdn/fdn_244`.\n- **Seams:** **G1** (fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent`), **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from graveyard +\n  one-shot exile-instead-of-graveyard replacement).\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.REACH`, base P/T 7/7. `cost_reduction(game)` =\n  count of cards in controller's graveyard whose `card_types` include INSTANT or SORCERY (engine\n  clamps to the {10} generic). `register_triggers`: `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, condition\n  `event.creature is self`, effect = `choose_yes_no` then pick a target instant/sorcery in your\n  graveyard, register a one-shot `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` on that card (redirect to exile),\n  then `cast_spell_free(game, controller, spell, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`.\n- **Edge/tests:** cost is {10} minus graveyard count, floored at 0 colored pips (none here);\n  attacking with empty graveyard / declining → nothing cast; the recast spell, after resolving,\n  goes to **exile** not graveyard (assert zone). Use `declare_attackers` helper to fire G1.\n\n### sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer — Creature {6}{B}{G} 5/5 — Affinity (uses G6)\n- **Clauses:** \"Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control). Flying,\n  deathtouch. Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n- **Analogue:** self-affinity `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n- **Seams:** self-part = `cost_reduction` hook (no engine change). Grant-to-others = **G6**.\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`. `cost_reduction(game)` =\n  number of creatures controller controls. Add a `grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`\n  method returning `creature_count` **iff** `card` has INSTANT/SORCERY type and is controlled by\n  the same player; G6 makes `get_cost_reduction` poll this across the battlefield.\n- **Edge/tests:** self cast cost drops by creature count (e.g. 3 creatures → {3}{B}{G}); an\n  instant you cast while Witherbloom is out is cheaper by creature count; a creature spell is not\n  affected; reduction never eats colored pips. Witherbloom counts itself? It's not yet on the\n  battlefield while being cast, so self-cast counts only *other* creatures — match RULEBOOK.\n\n### sos_97 — Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — Planeswalker {1}{B}{B}, loyalty 3 (uses G7, G9)\n- **Clauses:** `+1: Surveil 2. −1: Any number of target players each discard a card. −2: Return\n  target creature card with MV ≤3 from your graveyard to the battlefield. −7: Flip five coins;\n  target opponent skips their next X turns (X = heads).`\n- **Analogue:** `cards/fdn/fdn_134` (loyalty abilities + targeting).\n- **Seams:** **G7** (surveil) for +1; existing `discard`/`choose_card` for −1; existing\n  `move_to_zone`→battlefield for −2; **G9** (skip turns + coin flips) for −7.\n- **Impl:** base `Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=3)`, `supertypes={LEGENDARY}`, subtype \"Ral\".\n  `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility(+1/−1/−2/−7, effect, desc)`.\n  - +1: `surveil(game, controller, 2)`.\n  - −1: choose any number of target players; each chosen player `choose_card` from hand → `discard`.\n  - −2: target a creature card in controller's graveyard with `mana_cost.cmc ≤ 3`; `move_to_zone`\n    it to controller's battlefield.\n  - −7: `heads = sum(flip_coin(game, controller) for _ in range(5))`; target opponent;\n    `game.skipped_turns[opp_seat] += heads`.\n- **Edge/tests:** loyalty arithmetic and sorcery-speed/once-per-turn already handled by\n  `engine/abilities.py`; test +1 surveil moves chosen cards to graveyard / keeps order; −2 only\n  legal for MV≤3 creature cards; −7 with scripted coin results skips exactly that many of the\n  opponent's turns (drive turns with `run_turn`). **−7 is the hardest part — do it last** (G9).\n\n### sos_13 — Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — {1}{W}{W} 3/3 // {W} — Prepared (uses G4)\n- **Clauses (front face, the creature):** \"When this enters, target player creates a 1/1 W/B\n  Inkling with flying. Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this becomes prepared.\n  (While prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell; doing so unprepares it.)\" The \"spell\" = the\n  `// Swords to Plowshares` half: `{W}` Instant — \"Exile target creature; its controller gains\n  life equal to its power.\"\n- **Analogue:** ETB token `cards/fdn` token-makers; copy via `copy_spell`/**G4**.\n- **Seams:** **G4** (cast a copy), `create_token`, replacement-free.\n- **Impl:** implement the **creature** as the canonical class (`Creature`, {1}{W}{W}, 3/3,\n  subtypes {Cat, Cleric}). `register_triggers` → `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` condition\n  `event card is self`: target player creates `1/1 white/black Inkling, flying` via\n  `game.create_token`; then if any opponent controls more creatures than controller, set\n  `self.prepared=True`. Provide the StP effect as a method `_stp_resolve(game, target_creature)`:\n  `game.exile(target)`, target's controller gains life = target's power. Expose a special action /\n  `get_activated_abilities` available while `self.prepared` and on battlefield (instant speed, no\n  mana — it's \"cast a copy ... without paying\") that targets a creature, runs `_stp_resolve`, and\n  sets `self.prepared=False`.\n- **Edge/tests:** ETB always makes the token; `prepared` only set when opponent has strictly more\n  creatures; using the prepared action exiles a creature, grants life = power, and clears\n  `prepared` (can't be used twice without re-preparing). **Ambiguous card** — keep the\n  interpretation above; if a staged test disagrees, adjust the trigger/special-action shape, not\n  the engine. Complex — schedule late.\n\n### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone — Sorcery — Lesson {5}{R}{R} — Paradigm (uses G3, G5, G4)\n- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of library until you exile cards with total MV ≥4. You may\n  cast any number of them without paying. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying at the beginning of\n  each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **Analogue:** free-cast `cast_spell_free`; scheduling `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n- **Seams:** **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from exile), **G3** (first main phase trigger), **G4/G5** (cast copy from exile).\n- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop top of controller's library into exile, summing\n  `mana_cost.cmc`, until sum ≥4 (or library empty); for each exiled card the controller may\n  `cast_spell_free(... from Zone.EXILE)`. **Paradigm:** override the spell's own move-to-graveyard\n  so it goes to exile instead (one-shot replacement, like sos_1); set a per-player flag\n  `controller.paradigm_<thisname>=True`; register a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger\n  (condition: controller's **precombat** main, i.e. event.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN and active player is\n  controller) that each turn offers to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n  (`cast_copy` of a fresh `StackObject`, or simply `cast_spell_free` a `copy.copy` from exile).\n- **Edge/tests:** stops as soon as total MV ≥4 (single MV-5 card stops immediately); casting the\n  exiled spells is optional and any subset; after first resolution the card sits in exile and a\n  copy becomes castable at each of your first main phases. Expert — schedule late.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 — Miracle grant (uses G10)\n- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2} (cast it\n  when you draw it if it's the first card drawn this turn, for {2}). At the beginning of each\n  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n\n---\n\n## Section 3 — Implementation order\n\nBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\nsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n\n**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n\n**Group A — no/low new engine (warm-up):**\n5. **sos_4** (Converge) — pure `on_resolve`; nothing new. *Validates targeting + colors_spent.*\n6. **sos_226** (casualty) — G2 + `copy_spell`. *First consumer of the cast trigger.*\n7. **sos_57** (Mana Sculpt) — G8 + G2(`mana_spent`) + G3. *Exercises counter + scheduled mana.*\n\n**Group B — graveyard/exile recasting & cost grants:**\n8. **sos_1** (Dawning Archaic) — G1 + G5 (free-cast + exile redirect). *Cost reduction + attack recast.*\n9. **sos_245** (Witherbloom) — `cost_reduction` self + G6 grant. *Cost-system extension.*\n\n**Group C — planeswalker (modes mostly easy; ultimate hard):**\n10. **sos_97** (Ral) — +1/−1/−2 via G7/discard/move (easy); **−7 via G9 last** (skip turns + coins).\n\n**Group D — hardest (copy/alt-cost/animation):**\n11. **sos_13** (Prepared) — G4 + ETB token + special action; ambiguous, isolate it.\n12. **sos_120** (Paradigm) — G3 + G5 + G4; exile-recast scheduling.\n13. **sos_201** (Lorehold/Miracle) — G10 (draw trigger + per-turn reset + alt-cost cast).\n14. **sos_257** (Great Hall) — G11 land animation + restricted mana + G2 trigger.\n\n*Rationale for ordering:* Group A proves the three core seams (G1–G3, G7, G8) against simple\non-resolve logic before anything depends on them in combination. Group B reuses the free-cast and\ncost-reduction machinery. The planeswalker is mid-pack because three of its four modes are trivial\nonce G7 exists; its ultimate (G9) is the one genuinely new subsystem, so defer it. Group D cards\neach introduce a self-contained hard mechanic (copying a spell, alt-cost casting on draw, type-layer\nanimation) and benefit from all earlier seams being stable.\n\n## Testing notes (apply throughout)\n- Put tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`; import `from cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <Class>`\n  and `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state`.\n- Use `DeterministicPlayer` scripts (via `create_game(..., scripts=...)`) to make `choose_*`,\n  coin flips, and \"may\" prompts deterministic.\n- After each engine seam, run `pytest` — `engine_tests/` must stay green (they're authoritative-style\n  regressions; your additive changes should not break them).\n","numLines":335,"startLine":1,"totalLines":335}}}
