{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards (collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257) in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`. This is **Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION)** following a `PLAN.md` written by a planning agent. Critical contract details (verbatim-important):\n   - The contract is the **requirements** (`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt`), NOT the plan. The plan is a guide/hypothesis to verify, not obey. When deviating from PLAN.md, jot a one-line note in PLAN.md.\n   - Use **TDD**: write one failing test through the public interface (`test_utils`), watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time). Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - **Guardrails (verbatim-important):** \"Test the real engine, never a stand-in: don't hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call `on_resolve()` directly, or script a player's internal queue.\" \"After each card and after any `engine/` change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a change that regresses it.\" \"Do not modify anything under `engine_tests/` (the grader uses its own authoritative copies).\"\n   - From AGENTS.md: \"Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only\" and \"do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`\" — \"Editing them ... will not change your score, it will only mislead you.\" \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions ... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\"\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Write per-card tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities, replacement effects, 7-layer continuous effects, combat, mana payment, planeswalker loyalty.\n   - TDD red-green-refactor, vertical tracer-bullet slicing.\n   - Converge (colors of mana spent → X), Casualty, Counterspell, Affinity, Surveil, Miracle, Prepared, Paradigm, Land animation, coin flips/skip turns.\n   - `Keyword` enum.Flag (FLYING, VIGILANCE, REACH, DEATHTOUCH, HASTE, DEFENDER); `CardType` enum; `ManaType` enum (incl. COLORLESS); `ManaCost.parse(\"...\")` with `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips`, `.hybrid`.\n   - `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` — `zone` is informational in the deterministic cast pipeline (not enumerated); only `filter_fn` is enforced.\n   - `DeterministicPlayer` pops answers from a script deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card; `.remaining_choices` property; `._script` deque (appendleft used by test_utils to prepend targets/attackers).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **PLAN.md** (`/workspace/PLAN.md`): Full plan read. Defines G1-G11 seams and per-card plans with implementation order: seams (G1,G2,G3,G7,G8) → sos_4 → sos_226 → sos_57 → sos_1 → sos_245 → sos_97 → sos_13 → sos_120 → sos_201 → sos_257.\n   - **engine/combat.py** — EDITED (G1). After the attacker-declaration loop in `declare_attackers_step` (~line 252), added:\n     ```python\n     # Fire \"whenever ~ attacks\" triggers for every declared attacker. ...\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     for attacker, defender in list(combat.attackers.items()):\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n             game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=defender)\n         )\n     ```\n     `_can_attack(creature)` (line 79): returns False if is_tapped, _cant_attack, DEFENDER, or (summoning_sick and not HASTE).\n   - **engine/casting.py** — EDITED (G2). In `cast_spell`, changed payment block to:\n     ```python\n     pool_before = player.mana_pool.total()\n     player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n     card.mana_spent = pool_before - player.mana_pool.total()\n     card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)\n     ```\n     And after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player))\n     ```\n     KEY FACTS: `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (line 254) free-casts from any zone. `_resolve_spell` (line 393) sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets` before calling on_resolve; then moves permanents STACK→BATTLEFIELD or instant/sorcery STACK→GRAVEYARD via `move_to_zone` WITHOUT a replacement_event (so graveyard-redirect replacements are NOT consulted). `get_cost_reduction` clamps to [0, mana_cost.generic].\n   - **engine/events.py** — EDITED (G3). Added after BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         phase: Any = None\n     ```\n     `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` and `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` exist. `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` with `.card` property.\n   - **engine/turn.py** — EDITED (G3). In `run_turn`, added before the CLEANUP elif:\n     ```python\n     elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(phase=game.phase))\n     ```\n   - **engine/stack.py** — EDITED (G8). Added `Stack.remove`:\n     ```python\n     def remove(self, obj: StackObject) -> bool:\n         for i, item in enumerate(self._items):\n             if item is obj:\n                 del self._items[i]\n                 return True\n         return False\n     ```\n     And `counter_spell` before `check_state_based_actions`:\n     ```python\n     def counter_spell(game: GameState, stack_object: StackObject) -> bool:\n         from engine.types import Zone\n         from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n         if not game.stack.remove(stack_object):\n             return False\n         card = stack_object.source\n         move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n         return True\n     ```\n     `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` (line 72) shallow-copies source, binds `_copy_resolve` (sets copied_card.chosen_targets then calls copied_card.on_resolve), returns StackObject (no zone movement). `priority_loop` resolves stack when both players pass.\n   - **engine/game.py** — EDITED (G7). Added `surveil` before `discard`:\n     ```python\n     def surveil(game: GameState, player: Player, n: int) -> None:\n         if n <= 0: return\n         library = player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n         graveyard = player.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD]\n         top_cards = list(reversed(library.top(n)))\n         for card in top_cards:\n             name = getattr(card, \"name\", \"card\")\n             if player.choose_yes_no(f\"Surveil: put {name} into your graveyard?\"):\n                 library.remove(card)\n                 graveyard.add(card)\n     ```\n     Helpers: `deal_damage(game, source, target, amount)` (line 116; players have `life`, creatures have `damage_marked`); `sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` (237); `exile(game, obj)` (267); `create_token(game, player, token)` (382); `draw_card` (294, increments cards_drawn_this_turn, never reset, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent). No gain_life helper — use `controller.life += X` directly.\n   - **engine/zones.py**: `move_to_zone` fallback (lines 245-249) searches all players for the zone containing the card. Only consults replacement effects when `replacement_event is not None and leaving_battlefield`. Fires ETB BEFORE register_triggers. `ZoneContainer`: index -1 = top; `top(n)` returns last n (bottom-to-top); `add(obj, \"top\"/\"bottom\")`.\n   - **engine/card.py**: `Creature.__init__(name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller, base_power, base_toughness)`; `.power`=modified_power+plus_one-minus_one; default `summoning_sick=True`. `Instant`/`Sorcery` add CardType. `CardImpl` hooks: can_cast, cost_reduction, on_cast, on_resolve (reads self.chosen_targets), get_targets, register_triggers, register_replacement_effects, get_activated_abilities, get_modes.\n   - **engine/player.py**: choice methods `choose_target(options, requirement)`, `choose(options, description)`, `choose_yes_no(prompt)`, `choose_card(cards, description)`, `assign_damage_order`. DeterministicPlayer pops from `_script` deque; `.remaining_choices`.\n   - **test_utils.py**: `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=(s1,s2))`; `set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)` (REPLACES zones, assigns owner/controller, does NOT call register_triggers; mana empties pool then adds); `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)` (sets sorcery timing, prepends targets to script, casts via engine, auto-resolves ENTIRE stack via `_resolve_top_of_stack`); `_resolve_top_of_stack(game)` (pops+on_resolve+SBA until empty); `declare_attackers(game, names)` (advances to combat, prepends attackers to active script, calls declare_attackers_step — does NOT resolve stack); `advance_to_phase`.\n   - **cards/fdn/fdn_245/card_impl.py**: AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger pattern; condition checks `event.creature is source`; uses ContinuousEffect P/T buff + ManaAbility.\n   - **cards/fdn/fdn_48/card_impl.py** (Refute): counterspell with `can_cast` (checks stack for a counterable spell), `get_targets` (StackObjects with zone=Zone.STACK, `getattr(obj,\"is_spell\",True)`), and a local