{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H9RaWSg7Vsybuoxq1h5JMN","type":"tool_result","content":"155\tdef activate_ability(\n156\t    game: GameState,\n157\t    player: Any,  # Player\n158\t    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance | LoyaltyAbilityInstance,\n159\t) -> None:\n160\t    \"\"\"Activate an ability.\n161\t\n162\t    Pipeline\n163\t    --------\n164\t    1. **Timing check** — mana abilities bypass timing entirely and\n165\t       resolve immediately.  Regular (non-mana) activated abilities\n166\t       can be activated whenever a player has priority (instant speed);\n167\t       priority enforcement is handled externally by\n168\t       ``priority_loop``, not here.  **Only loyalty abilities** carry\n169\t       a sorcery-speed restriction.\n170\t    2. **Pay costs** — invoke the ability's cost callable.  For loyalty\n171\t       abilities, adjust loyalty counters and enforce once-per-turn.\n172\t    3. **Resolve or push to stack** — mana abilities resolve\n173\t       immediately; all other abilities are pushed onto the game stack\n174\t       as :class:`StackObject` instances.\n175\t\n176\t    Parameters:\n177\t        game: The current game state.\n178\t        player: The player activating the ability.\n179\t        ability: The ability to activate (an\n180\t            :class:`ActivatedAbilityInstance` or\n181\t            :class:`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`).\n182\t\n183\t    Raises:\n184\t        AbilityError: If the activation is illegal (timing, cost, or\n185\t            once-per-turn restriction).\n186\t    \"\"\"\n187\t    if isinstance(ability, LoyaltyAbilityInstance):\n188\t        _activate_loyalty_ability(game, player, ability)\n189\t    elif isinstance(ability, ActivatedAbilityInstance):\n190\t        _activate_regular_ability(game, player, ability)\n191\t    else:\n192\t        raise AbilityError(f\"Unknown ability type: {type(ability)}\")\n193\t\n194\t\n195\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t# Internal helpers\n197\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n198\t\n199\tdef _activate_regular_ability(\n200\t    game: GameState,\n201\t    player: Any,\n202\t    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance,\n203\t) -> None:\n204\t    \"\"\"Activate a regular (non-loyalty) activated ability.\"\"\"\n205\t    # 1. Check \"can't activate\" restriction (e.g. Arrest).\n206\t    if getattr(ability.source, \"_cant_activate\", False):\n207\t        raise AbilityError(\n208\t            \"Cannot activate ability — source's activated abilities are suppressed\"\n209\t        )\n210\t\n211\t    # 2. Pay costs\n212\t    cost_paid = ability.cost(game, ability.source)\n213\t    if not cost_paid:\n214\t        raise AbilityError(\"Cannot activate ability — cost could not be paid\")\n215\t\n216\t    # 3. Resolve or push\n217\t    if ability.is_mana_ability:\n218\t        # Mana abilities resolve immediately without using the stack.\n219\t        ability.effect(game)\n220\t    else:\n221\t        # Push to stack for resolution.\n222\t        stack_obj = StackObject(\n223\t            source=ability.source,\n224\t            controller=player,\n225\t            on_resolve=ability.effect,\n226\t            is_mana_ability=False,\n227\t        )\n228\t        game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n229\t\n230\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"8197d4c3-120b-4a26-b190-24a921876d48","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:07:08.430Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/engine/abilities.py","content":"def activate_ability(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Any,  # Player\n    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance | LoyaltyAbilityInstance,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Activate an ability.\n\n    Pipeline\n    --------\n    1. **Timing check** — mana abilities bypass timing entirely and\n       resolve immediately.  Regular (non-mana) activated abilities\n       can be activated whenever a player has priority (instant speed);\n       priority enforcement is handled externally by\n       ``priority_loop``, not here.  **Only loyalty abilities** carry\n       a sorcery-speed restriction.\n    2. **Pay costs** — invoke the ability's cost callable.  For loyalty\n       abilities, adjust loyalty counters and enforce once-per-turn.\n    3. **Resolve or push to stack** — mana abilities resolve\n       immediately; all other abilities are pushed onto the game stack\n       as :class:`StackObject` instances.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player activating the ability.\n        ability: The ability to activate (an\n            :class:`ActivatedAbilityInstance` or\n            :class:`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`).\n\n    Raises:\n        AbilityError: If the activation is illegal (timing, cost, or\n            once-per-turn restriction).\n    \"\"\"\n    if isinstance(ability, LoyaltyAbilityInstance):\n        _activate_loyalty_ability(game, player, ability)\n    elif isinstance(ability, ActivatedAbilityInstance):\n        _activate_regular_ability(game, player, ability)\n    else:\n        raise AbilityError(f\"Unknown ability type: {type(ability)}\")\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Internal helpers\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _activate_regular_ability(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Any,\n    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Activate a regular (non-loyalty) activated ability.\"\"\"\n    # 1. Check \"can't activate\" restriction (e.g. Arrest).\n    if getattr(ability.source, \"_cant_activate\", False):\n        raise AbilityError(\n            \"Cannot activate ability — source's activated abilities are suppressed\"\n        )\n\n    # 2. Pay costs\n    cost_paid = ability.cost(game, ability.source)\n    if not cost_paid:\n        raise AbilityError(\"Cannot activate ability — cost could not be paid\")\n\n    # 3. Resolve or push\n    if ability.is_mana_ability:\n        # Mana abilities resolve immediately without using the stack.\n        ability.effect(game)\n    else:\n        # Push to stack for resolution.\n        stack_obj = StackObject(\n            source=ability.source,\n            controller=player,\n            on_resolve=ability.effect,\n            is_mana_ability=False,\n        )\n        game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n\n","numLines":76,"startLine":155,"totalLines":273}}}
