{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   This is **Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION)** of a two-phase task: implement 10 SOS Magic: The Gathering cards (collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257) in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py`, each with a per-card test file at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`. A `PLAN.md` written by a planning agent is a guide/hypothesis to verify — NOT the contract. The contract is the requirements (`card_spec.json` + `RULEBOOK.txt`). Critical verbatim constraints (still in force):\n   - Use **TDD**: write one failing test through the public interface (test_utils), watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time). Do NOT write all tests up front.\n   - \"**Test the real engine, never a stand-in:** don't hand-construct internal events, pop the stack and call `on_resolve()` directly, or script a player's internal queue.\"\n   - \"After each card and after any `engine/` change, run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never ship a change that regresses it.\" \"Do not modify anything under `engine_tests/` (the grader uses its own authoritative copies).\"\n   - From AGENTS.md: \"Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only\" and \"do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`\" — \"Editing them ... will not change your score, it will only mislead you.\" \"**Additive-only engine modifications** — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions ... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\"\n   - When deviating from PLAN.md, jot a one-line note in PLAN.md.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine: zones, LIFO stack, triggered abilities (pushed to stack via `trigger_manager.fire_event`, resolved when stack pops), activated/loyalty abilities, replacement effects, continuous effects, combat, mana payment, planeswalker loyalty.\n   - TDD red-green-refactor, vertical tracer-bullet slicing.\n   - Mechanics: Converge (colors_spent → X), Casualty, Counterspell, Affinity (self + granted to other spells), Surveil, coin flips, skip turns, Prepared (preparation cards / prepare spell), Miracle, Paradigm, land animation.\n   - `Keyword` enum.Flag (FLYING, VIGILANCE, REACH, DEATHTOUCH, HASTE, DEFENDER, DOUBLE_STRIKE, FLASH); `CardType` enum; `Supertype.LEGENDARY`; `ManaType` enum (incl. COLORLESS, WHITE, BLACK, GREEN, RED, BLUE); `ManaCost.parse(\"...\")` with `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips`, `.hybrid`.\n   - `TargetRequirement(filter_fn, description, zone)` — only `filter_fn` enforced in cast pipeline.\n   - `DeterministicPlayer`: pops answers from `_script` deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card; `.remaining_choices`; tests use `_script.append/.extend/.appendleft` and can set arbitrary attributes (e.g. `_coin_flips`).\n   - Engine seams completed this session: **G6** (affinity granted to other spells via `grants_cost_reduction` polled in `get_cost_reduction`), **G9** (`flip_coin` + `skipped_turns`). Previously done: G1 (AttacksTriggeredEvent fire), G2 (mana_spent/colors_spent + SpellCastTriggeredEvent), G3 (BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent), G7 (surveil), G8 (counter_spell/Stack.remove/copy_spell). G5 implemented card-locally (wrap-StackObject, not replacement effect).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py`** (CREATED, 8 tests pass):\n     `TheDawningArchaic(Creature)`, name \"The Dawning Archaic\", mana_cost {10}, subtypes {Avatar}, supertypes {LEGENDARY}, keywords REACH, base 7/7. `cost_reduction(game)` = count of instant/sorcery cards in controller's graveyard (engine clamps to generic 10). `register_triggers` registers AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger, condition `event.creature is source`; effect (when trigger resolves): if controller has eligible instant/sorcery in graveyard and `choose_yes_no` true, `choose_card`, `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`, then `_redirect_to_exile`. `_redirect_to_exile` grabs `game.stack.peek()`, wraps its `on_resolve`: run original, then if card landed in owner's graveyard, `exile(game, spell_card)`.\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`** (CREATED, 8 pass): `LifeGainBolt(Instant)` (+3 life, {R}, no targets). Property tests, cost_reduction counting, real reduced cast ({10}-4=6 colorless), attack free-cast→exile (script `[True, bolt]` after `archaic.summoning_sick=False` and `archaic.register_triggers(game)`, then `declare_attackers(game,[\"The Dawning Archaic\"])` + `_resolve_top_of_stack`), and decline case.\n   - **`/workspace/engine/casting.py`** (EDITED, G6): In `get_cost_reduction`, after computing `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)` and restoring controller, added:\n     ```python\n     for owner in game.players:\n         for perm in owner.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD].get_all():\n             granter = getattr(perm, \"grants_cost_reduction\", None)\n             if granter is None:\n                 continue\n             raw += granter(game, card, controller)\n     ```\n     Then `generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0; return max(0, min(raw, generic))`. (Zone already imported.)\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`** (CREATED, 8 tests pass): `WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)` {6}{B}{G}, subtypes {Elder,Dragon}, supertypes {LEGENDARY}, keywords FLYING|DEATHTOUCH, 5/5. `cost_reduction(game)` = `_creature_count(game, controller)`. `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller)`: returns 0 unless `controller is self.controller` AND card is instant/sorcery, else `_creature_count(game, self.controller)`. Module helpers `_is_instant_or_sorcery(card)` and `_creature_count(game, controller)`.\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`** (CREATED, 8 pass): `BigSpell(Instant)` {4} no-op; `_creature(name, owner)` helper. Self-affinity cost_reduction, reduced real cast ({6}{B}{G}-2), granted-affinity reduced instant cast, and two negative tests using `pytest.raises(TestSetupError)` (imported from test_utils): creature spell not affected, opponent's spell not affected.\n   - **`/workspace/engine/game.py`** (EDITED, G9): Added `import random` at top. Added `flip_coin(game, player) -> bool` before `discard`:\n     ```python\n     def flip_coin(game, player):\n         scripted = getattr(player, \"_coin_flips\", None)\n         if scripted:\n             if hasattr(scripted, \"popleft\"):\n                 return bool(scripted.popleft())\n             return bool(scripted.pop(0))\n         return random.choice((True, False))\n     ```\n     (heads=True). Existing helpers: `surveil`, `discard`, `create_token`, `deal_damage`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card`.\n   - **`/workspace/engine/game_state.py`** (EDITED, G9): In `__init__` added `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}`. In `advance_phase` end-of-turn branch, replaced direct `active_player_index` assignment with `candidate` (from extra_turns.pop(0) or _normal_next_index toggle), then:\n     ```python\n     guard = 0\n     while self.skipped_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0 and guard < 8:\n         self.skipped_turns[candidate] -= 1\n         candidate = 1 - candidate\n         guard += 1\n     self.active_player_index = candidate\n     self.priority_player_index = self.active_player_index\n     ```\n     Inert for all existing tests (skipped_turns empty by default). `_TURN_SEQUENCE[-1]` = (Phase.ENDING, Step.CLEANUP).\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`** (CREATED, 8 tests pass): `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` {1}{B}{B}, starting_loyalty 3, supertypes {LEGENDARY}, subtype \"Ral\". `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns 4 `LoyaltyAbility(+1/-1/-2/-7, effect, desc)`. +1: `surveil(game, ctrl, 2)`. −1: for each player, `ctrl.choose_yes_no` to target; if yes, that player `choose_card` from hand → `discard`. −2: eligible = creatures in ctrl graveyard with `_mana_value(c) <= 3`; `ctrl.choose_card` → `move_to_zone(game, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)`. −7: `heads = sum(1 for _ in range(5) if flip_coin(game, ctrl))`; opp = other player; `game.skipped_turns[seat] += heads`.\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`** (CREATED, 8 pass): Helper `_activate(game, player, pw, index)` calls `clear_loyalty_tracking()`, sets active/priority index + PRECOMBAT_MAIN/step=None, builds `LoyaltyAbilityInstance(source=pw, controller=player, loyalty_cost=ab.loyalty_cost, effect=ab.effect)`, `activate_ability`, `_resolve_top_of_stack`. Tests for each ability + a skip-rotation integration test (`game.skipped_turns={1:1}`, `game._normal_next_index=1`, set phase/step to `_TURN_SEQUENCE[-1]`, `game.advance_phase()`, assert active==0 and skip consumed). Uses `_coin_flips = deque([True,True,True,False,False])` for −7 (3 heads, loyalty set to 7 first).\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`** (CREATED, tests NOT yet run): `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)` {1}{W}{W}, subtypes {Cat,Cleric}, 3/3, `self.prepared=False`. `register_triggers(self, game)` is used as the entry hook — it calls `self._on_enter(game)`. `_on_enter`: `target_player = ctrl.choose(list(game.players), ...)` (default ctrl), creates Inkling token (1/1, subtypes {Inkling}, keywords FLYING) via `create_token`, then if `opp_max > my_count` sets `self.prepared=True` (`_creature_count` helper). `get_activated_abilities(self, game)`: returns `[]` unless `self.prepared`; else one `ActivatedAbility(cost=_cost, effect=_effect, desc=...)`. `_cost(game, src)`: pays {W} from controller's mana pool (returns False if can't pay), sets `src.prepared=False`, returns True. `_effect` calls `_swords_to_plowshares`: gather all creatures, `ctrl.choose_card`, `exile(game, target)`, `target_controller.life += max(0, power)`.\n   - **`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`** (CREATED, NOT yet run): Properties; `TestEnters` casts via `cast_spell(game, 0, \"Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\", targets=[p1])` and asserts Inkling token / prepared logic; `TestPreparedSpell` uses helper `_activate_stp` building `ActivatedAbilityInstance(source=emeritus, controller=player, cost=ability.cost, effect=ability.effect)` + `activate_ability` + `_resolve_top_of_stack`. Tests: no ability while unprepared; prepared exiles victim (4/4) and grants p2 +4 life with mana {WHITE:1} and `p1._script.append(victim)`, asserts prepared False after; consumed-only-once.\n   - **`/workspace/PLAN.md`** (EDITED): Added deviation notes under sos_1 (G5 wrap-StackObject) and under sos_97 (G9 built — flip_coin/skipped_turns details).\n   - **Engine read facts**: `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` free-casts (no mana/timing), pushes StackObject. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets`, calls on_resolve, then move_to_zone STACK→BATTLEFIELD (permanents) or STACK→GRAVEYARD (instant/sorcery) WITHOUT replacement_event. `get_cost_reduction` clamps to [0, generic]. `zones.move_to_zone` entering-battlefield order: add to battlefield → fire EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent → register_triggers → register_replacement_effects (so SELF-ETB triggers DON'T fire on own entry). `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller)`. `activate_ability(game, player, ability)` dispatches to `_activate_loyalty_ability` (sorcery timing, once-per-turn via `clear_loyalty_tracking`/turn_number, pay loyalty, push effect to stack) or `_activate_regular_ability` (checks `_cant_activate`, `ability.cost(game, source)->bool`, pushes effect to stack or resolves if mana). `ActivatedAbility(cost, effect, description)` in engine.card; `ActivatedAbilityInstance`/`LoyaltyAbilityInstance` in engine.abilities. `test_utils.cast_spell` re-wraps engine exceptions as `TestSetupError`. `_resolve_top_of_stack` pops+on_resolve+SBA until empty. `declare_attackers` prepends attacker list to active script and calls `declare_attackers_step` (fires AttacksTriggeredEvent per attacker AFTER registering all); `_can_attack` rejects summoning_sick (unless HASTE)/tapped/DEFENDER.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **sos_245 negative tests not raising CastingError**: `test_creature_spell_not_affected` and `test_opponents_spell_not_affected` used `pytest.raises(CastingError)` but `test_utils.cast_spell` wraps engine exceptions in `TestSetupError` (`raise TestSetupError(...) from exc`). Fixed: imported `TestSetupError` from test_utils and `sed`-replaced `pytest.raises(CastingError)` → `pytest.raises(TestSetupError)`. All 8 passed.\n   - **G6 useless no-op loop**: Initially added a pointless `for perm in owner.zones[Zone.STACK].get_all(): pass` loop; removed it immediately, leaving only the BATTLEFIELD granter loop.\n   - No other errors; sos_1, sos_245, sos_97 all green; engine stayed at 1145 passed after every change.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - G5 deviation (carried over): `_resolve_spell` doesn't pass a replacement_event, so graveyard redirect can't use replacement effects; instead wrap the StackObject's on_resolve to exile after resolution (sos_1; sos_120 will reuse).\n   - G6: chose to poll all battlefield permanents for an optional `grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` method in `get_cost_reduction` (the granter decides applicability). Single source of truth — a spell's own `cost_reduction` is separate from granted reductions.\n   - G9: made `flip_coin` deterministic-testable via a `player._coin_flips` sequence attribute (no test_utils modification needed); made `skipped_turns` a dict defaulting to `{}` so the new advance_phase branch is inert for existing tests.\n   - Loyalty/activated abilities tested through the real engine `activate_ability` + `*AbilityInstance` (legit public API), resolving off the stack — not popping/calling on_resolve directly. Targets are chosen at resolution via controller choose methods (engine has no built-in loyalty/ability targeting).\n   - sos_13 ETB problem: ETB fires before register_triggers (engine design), so a self-ETB trigger misses its own entry. Decided register_triggers IS the entry hook and run the ETB effect directly there, enabling a real-cast test. Used the prepared spell as `get_activated_abilities` returning an `ActivatedAbility` only while `self.prepared`. This is the ambiguous-card interpretation per PLAN; guardrail says adjust the special-action shape (not engine) if a staged test disagrees.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (Continuation prompt) \"Continue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with 'I'll continue' or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\" (preceded by the prior-session summary and system-reminders that several files had been read).\n   - Multiple system-generated reminders: \"The task tools haven't been used recently... consider using TaskCreate/TaskUpdate...\" (not real user feedback; informational).\n   - The initial system reminders showed Read results for sos_57/sos_226/sos_4 card_impl and tests files.\n   - (Final) The summary request: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - No new security-sensitive constraints beyond those already in force (engine_tests/ read-only; don't modify FDN reference tests; additive-only engine edits; don't modify test_utils unnecessarily).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **sos_13** (#8, in_progress): run tests, fix failures, run engine suite, mark complete, note any deviation.\n   - **sos_120** (#9): Improvisation Capstone — Sorcery (Lesson {5}{R}{R}) — Paradigm. Us