{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZt6JgqdkPcBXuCfqntobY","type":"tool_result","content":"241\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone — Sorcery — Lesson {5}{R}{R} — Paradigm (uses G3, G5, G4)\n242\t- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of library until you exile cards with total MV ≥4. You may\n243\t  cast any number of them without paying. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n244\t  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying at the beginning of\n245\t  each of your first main phases.)\"\n246\t- **Analogue:** free-cast `cast_spell_free`; scheduling `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n247\t- **Seams:** **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from exile), **G3** (first main phase trigger), **G4/G5** (cast copy from exile).\n248\t- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop top of controller's library into exile, summing\n249\t  `mana_cost.cmc`, until sum ≥4 (or library empty); for each exiled card the controller may\n250\t  `cast_spell_free(... from Zone.EXILE)`. **Paradigm:** override the spell's own move-to-graveyard\n251\t  so it goes to exile instead (one-shot replacement, like sos_1); set a per-player flag\n252\t  `controller.paradigm_<thisname>=True`; register a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger\n253\t  (condition: controller's **precombat** main, i.e. event.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN and active player is\n254\t  controller) that each turn offers to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n255\t  (`cast_copy` of a fresh `StackObject`, or simply `cast_spell_free` a `copy.copy` from exile).\n256\t- **Edge/tests:** stops as soon as total MV ≥4 (single MV-5 card stops immediately); casting the\n257\t  exiled spells is optional and any subset; after first resolution the card sits in exile and a\n258\t  copy becomes castable at each of your first main phases. Expert — schedule late.\n259\t\n260\t### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 — Miracle grant (uses G10)\n261\t- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2} (cast it\n262\t  when you draw it if it's the first card drawn this turn, for {2}). At the beginning of each\n263\t  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n264\t- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n265\t- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n266\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n267\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n268\t  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n269\t  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n270\t    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n271\t    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n272\t  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n273\t    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n274\t- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n275\t  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n276\t  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n277\t\n278\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n279\t- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n280\t  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n281\t  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n282\t- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n283\t- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n284\t  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n285\t- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n286\t  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n287\t  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n288\t    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n289\t    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n290\t  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n291\t  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n292\t  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n293\t  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n294\t- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n295\t  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n296\t  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n297\t  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n298\t\n299\t---\n300\t\n301\t## Section 3 — Implementation order\n302\t\n303\tBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\n304\tsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n305\t\n306\t**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n307\t1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n308\t2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n309\t   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n310\t3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n311\t4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n312\t   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n313\t   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n314\t\n315\t**Group A — no/low new engine (warm-up):**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"7768530a-6be3-44b5-ba38-3af44d1f48e3","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:13:20.127Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone — Sorcery — Lesson {5}{R}{R} — Paradigm (uses G3, G5, G4)\n- **Clauses:** \"Exile cards from top of library until you exile cards with total MV ≥4. You may\n  cast any number of them without paying. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying at the beginning of\n  each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **Analogue:** free-cast `cast_spell_free`; scheduling `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n- **Seams:** **G5** (`cast_spell_free` from exile), **G3** (first main phase trigger), **G4/G5** (cast copy from exile).\n- **Impl:** base `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop top of controller's library into exile, summing\n  `mana_cost.cmc`, until sum ≥4 (or library empty); for each exiled card the controller may\n  `cast_spell_free(... from Zone.EXILE)`. **Paradigm:** override the spell's own move-to-graveyard\n  so it goes to exile instead (one-shot replacement, like sos_1); set a per-player flag\n  `controller.paradigm_<thisname>=True`; register a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` trigger\n  (condition: controller's **precombat** main, i.e. event.phase==PRECOMBAT_MAIN and active player is\n  controller) that each turn offers to cast a copy of this card from exile for free\n  (`cast_copy` of a fresh `StackObject`, or simply `cast_spell_free` a `copy.copy` from exile).\n- **Edge/tests:** stops as soon as total MV ≥4 (single MV-5 card stops immediately); casting the\n  exiled spells is optional and any subset; after first resolution the card sits in exile and a\n  copy becomes castable at each of your first main phases. Expert — schedule late.\n\n### sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — Creature {3}{R}{W} 5/5 — Miracle grant (uses G10)\n- **Clauses:** \"Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2} (cast it\n  when you draw it if it's the first card drawn this turn, for {2}). At the beginning of each\n  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n\n---\n\n## Section 3 — Implementation order\n\nBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\nsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n\n**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n\n**Group A — no/low new engine (warm-up):**","numLines":75,"startLine":241,"totalLines":347}}}
