{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0112dfpBN88cNRNG24KCpqng","type":"tool_result","content":"5403\t702.192. Paradigm\n5404\t\n5405\t702.192a Paradigm represents two spell abilities, one of which creates a delayed triggered ability. Paradigm means “If this is the first time a spell you control with this spell’s name has resolved this game, at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, create a copy of this object in exile. You may cast the copy without paying its mana cost” and “Exile this spell.” See rule 707.10.\n5406\t\n5407\t703. Turn-Based Actions\n5408\t\n5409\t703.1. Turn-based actions are game actions that happen automatically when certain steps or phases begin, or when each step and phase ends. Turn-based actions don’t use the stack.\n5410\t\n5411\t703.1a Abilities that watch for a specified step or phase to begin are triggered abilities, not turn-based actions. (See rule 603, “Handling Triggered Abilities.”)\n5412\t\n5413\t703.2. Turn-based actions are not controlled by any player.\n5414\t\n5415\t703.3. Whenever a step or phase begins, if it’s a step or phase that has any turn-based action associated with it, those turn-based actions are automatically dealt with first. This happens before state-based actions are checked, before triggered abilities are put on the stack, and before players receive priority.\n5416\t\n5417\t703.4. The turn-based actions are as follows:\n5418\t\n5419\t703.4a Immediately after the untap step begins, all phased-in permanents with phasing that the active player controls phase out, and all phased-out permanents that the active player controlled when they phased out phase in. This all happens simultaneously. See rule 502.1.\n5420\t\n5421\t703.4b Immediately after the phasing action has been completed during the untap step, if the game has either the day or night designation, it checks to see whether that designation should change. If it’s neither day nor night, this check doesn’t happen. See rule 502.2.\n5422\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"d7541d58-7022-4211-a64f-b5cf3ce66555","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:13:29.417Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/RULEBOOK.txt","content":"702.192. Paradigm\n\n702.192a Paradigm represents two spell abilities, one of which creates a delayed triggered ability. Paradigm means “If this is the first time a spell you control with this spell’s name has resolved this game, at the beginning of each of your precombat main phases for the rest of the game, create a copy of this object in exile. You may cast the copy without paying its mana cost” and “Exile this spell.” See rule 707.10.\n\n703. Turn-Based Actions\n\n703.1. Turn-based actions are game actions that happen automatically when certain steps or phases begin, or when each step and phase ends. Turn-based actions don’t use the stack.\n\n703.1a Abilities that watch for a specified step or phase to begin are triggered abilities, not turn-based actions. (See rule 603, “Handling Triggered Abilities.”)\n\n703.2. Turn-based actions are not controlled by any player.\n\n703.3. Whenever a step or phase begins, if it’s a step or phase that has any turn-based action associated with it, those turn-based actions are automatically dealt with first. This happens before state-based actions are checked, before triggered abilities are put on the stack, and before players receive priority.\n\n703.4. The turn-based actions are as follows:\n\n703.4a Immediately after the untap step begins, all phased-in permanents with phasing that the active player controls phase out, and all phased-out permanents that the active player controlled when they phased out phase in. This all happens simultaneously. See rule 502.1.\n\n703.4b Immediately after the phasing action has been completed during the untap step, if the game has either the day or night designation, it checks to see whether that designation should change. If it’s neither day nor night, this check doesn’t happen. See rule 502.2.\n","numLines":20,"startLine":5403,"totalLines":9323}}}
