nstraints beyond those already in force (engine_tests/ read-only; don't modify FDN reference tests; additive-only engine edits; don't modify test_utils unnecessarily; card class must stay in cards/sos/{id}/card_impl.py).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **sos_257** (task #11, in_progress): Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land animation (G11). Implement card_impl + tests. Then run engine suite, note deviation, mark complete.\n   - This is the LAST of the 10 cards. After it, all tasks (#1–#11) will be complete.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I was implementing **sos_257 (Great Hall of the Biblioplex)**, task #11, in_progress. I had finished READING the engine support needed (Land base, basic_lands.py ManaAbility pattern, continuous_effects.py Layer/SubLayer/EffectManager, Creature P/T, fdn_109 and fdn_168 continuous-effect examples, abilities.py activate_ability) and was reading `engine/abilities.py` (offset 129, `_activate_regular_ability`) to confirm the activated-ability resolution path. **No sos_257 test or implementation code has been written yet** — the card_impl.py is still the TODO stub. I had designed the plan: `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)` with creature P/T plumbing (base_power=0, base_toughness=0, modified_power/modified_toughness, plus_one/minus_one counters, power/toughness properties, overridden `_reset_characteristics`); `get_mana_abilities()` returning `{T}: Add {C}` and `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` (color chosen via `ctrl.choose`, restriction unenforced+documented); `get_activated_abilities(self, game)` returning a `{5}` ability (guarded by `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`) whose effect registers permanent ContinuousEffects (Layer.TYPE adds CREATURE + \"Wizard\" subtype; Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS SET_PT sets modified_power=2, modified_toughness=4) and registers a SpellCastTriggeredEvent pump trigger adding an end-of-turn Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS MODIFY_PT +1/+0 effect, then calls `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin sos_257 with the TDD properties tracer bullet (write a failing properties test + minimal Land implementation), then iterate: mana abilities → {5} animation (using `activate_ability` + `ActivatedAbilityInstance` and `game.effect_manager.apply_all`) → the +1/+0 cast-trigger pump. This directly continues task #11. Per the user's standing TDD instruction: \"write one failing test through the public interface (test_utils), watch it fail for the right reason, write minimal code to pass, repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time).\" Concretely, create `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` with a `TestProperties` test (assert it's a Land, name \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\", no mana cost) and a minimal `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)` impl, run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py -q` to confirm red→green, then continue with mana/animation/pump tracer bullets, running `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` after any engine change (G11 must keep engine at 1145).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"9b236ded-0191-45ef-a213-67810074a0de","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:29:03.003Z","isSynthetic":true}
