{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPFYafXdZTpyQCsFYXG677","type":"tool_result","content":"270\t  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n271\t- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n272\t- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n273\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n274\t- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n275\t  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n276\t  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n277\t    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n278\t    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n279\t  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n280\t    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n281\t- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n282\t  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n283\t  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n284\t- **DEVIATION (built):** G10 done as two additive engine pieces: (1) `cast_for_cost(game, player,\n285\t  card, cost, from_zone=HAND)` in `engine/casting.py` — mirrors `cast_spell` but pays a supplied\n286\t  ManaCost and skips the timing check (window granted by the miracle trigger); fires\n287\t  SpellCastTriggeredEvent. (2) per-turn reset of `cards_drawn_this_turn` for all players added to\n288\t  `_do_untap_step` in `engine/turn.py` (the increment + DrawsCardTriggeredEvent fire already existed\n289\t  in `game.draw_card`). Both inert for the 1145 engine tests. Trigger effects read event data via\n290\t  the codebase's capture-on-condition pattern (cf. fdn_111). Tested by calling real `draw_card` /\n291\t  firing `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` then resolving the stack.\n292\t\n293\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n294\t- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n295\t  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n296\t  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n297\t- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n298\t- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n299\t  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n300\t- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n301\t  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n302\t  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n303\t    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n304\t    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n305\t  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n306\t  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n307\t  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n308\t  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n309\t- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n310\t  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n311\t  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n312\t  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n313\t\n314\t---\n315\t\n316\t## Section 3 — Implementation order\n317\t\n318\tBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\n319\tsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n320\t\n321\t**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n322\t1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n323\t2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n324\t   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n325\t3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n326\t4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n327\t   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n328\t   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n329\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1404691a-99e3-4d00-a347-c654df745e5c","uuid":"e55f0f1d-d6d0-4b14-ae70-69faa72b8a66","timestamp":"2026-06-04T03:29:30.906Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"  opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card; if you do, draw a card.\"\n- **Analogue:** upkeep trigger pattern fdn cards; draw event already fired by `game.draw_card`.\n- **Seams:** **G10** (reset `cards_drawn_this_turn` per turn + `cast_for_cost` + draw trigger);\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` for the loot.\n- **Impl:** base `Creature`, `keywords=Keyword.FLYING|Keyword.HASTE`, 5/5, subtypes {Elder, Dragon},\n  legendary. `register_triggers`:\n  - `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, condition: `event.player is controller` AND\n    `controller.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND drawn card has INSTANT/SORCERY type. Effect:\n    `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `cast_for_cost(game, controller, event.card, ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"))`.\n  - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, condition: active player is an opponent (not controller).\n    Effect: `choose_yes_no`; if yes, `discard` a chosen card then `draw_card`.\n- **Edge/tests:** miracle offered only on the **first** draw of the turn (verify the per-turn\n  reset), only for instant/sorcery, only while Lorehold is on the battlefield; declining leaves the\n  card in hand. The opponent-upkeep loot is a \"may\", and only on opponents' upkeeps. Expert.\n- **DEVIATION (built):** G10 done as two additive engine pieces: (1) `cast_for_cost(game, player,\n  card, cost, from_zone=HAND)` in `engine/casting.py` — mirrors `cast_spell` but pays a supplied\n  ManaCost and skips the timing check (window granted by the miracle trigger); fires\n  SpellCastTriggeredEvent. (2) per-turn reset of `cards_drawn_this_turn` for all players added to\n  `_do_untap_step` in `engine/turn.py` (the increment + DrawsCardTriggeredEvent fire already existed\n  in `game.draw_card`). Both inert for the 1145 engine tests. Trigger effects read event data via\n  the codebase's capture-on-condition pattern (cf. fdn_111). Tested by calling real `draw_card` /\n  firing `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` then resolving the stack.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — Land — animation (uses G2, G11)\n- **Clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color; spend only to cast an\n  instant/sorcery. {5}: If this isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever\n  you cast an instant/sorcery, this gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **Analogue:** `engine/basic_lands.py` (mana abilities); animation via `ContinuousEffect`.\n- **Seams:** **G11** (TYPE+P/T continuous effects, optional restricted-mana tag), **G2** (the\n  granted +1/+0 cast-trigger).\n- **Impl:** base `Land`. `get_mana_abilities()`:\n  - `{T}: Add {C}` → tap cost, `mana_pool.add(ManaType.COLORLESS, 1)`.\n  - `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add any color` → tap + `controller.life -= 1`; add a chosen color. Tag the\n    mana as instant/sorcery-restricted **if** you add minimal restriction support (G11); otherwise\n    document the simplification (add untagged) and note the restriction is unenforced.\n  `get_activated_abilities()`: `{5}` ability, condition `CardType.CREATURE not in self.card_types`,\n  effect adds permanent `ContinuousEffect`s (Layer.TYPE: add CREATURE + subtype \"Wizard\";\n  Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS: set base 2/4) and registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger\n  (condition: controller casts an instant/sorcery) giving `self` +1/+0 until end of turn.\n- **Edge/tests:** both mana abilities produce mana and the life-payment one costs 1 life; {5}\n  animation makes it a 2/4 creature that is still a Land (assert both card types) and only once\n  (guard on already-creature); after animation, casting an instant/sorcery pumps it +1/+0 that\n  turn (needs G2). If restricted mana is left unenforced, say so in the test comments. Complex.\n\n---\n\n## Section 3 — Implementation order\n\nBuild the shared engine seams first (cheap, additive, unblock many cards), then cards\nsimplest→hardest. Each group lists its rationale.\n\n**Step 0 — Shared engine seams (do these first):**\n1. **G1** fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (combat.py) — one line, unblocks sos_1.\n2. **G2** fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` + record `card.mana_spent` (casting.py) — unblocks\n   sos_226/sos_257/sos_57.\n3. **G3** `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` event + fire in run_turn — unblocks sos_57/sos_120.\n4. **G7** `surveil` helper, **G8** `counter_spell` helper — small, isolated, unblock sos_97/sos_57.\n   *Rationale:* all additive, low-risk, and every later card leans on one of these. Add a focused\n   engine_tests-style check in your own SOS tests (don't touch `engine_tests/`).\n","numLines":60,"startLine":270,"totalLines":362}}}
